module bankr-pr-local-rules.local-rules

import core.states.puerto-rico.{ frbp9006-puerto-rico }
import frbp.events.{ FirstMeetingDate, OrderForReliefEntered, PetitionFiled }

// The Bankr. D.P.R. court's own periods, counted under FRBP 9006(a). The
// FRBP and statutory periods are lit/frbp's and the Code's and are not
// declared again: the 21 days' notice of a sale (P.R. LBR 6004-1(b); FRBP
// 2002(a)(2)), the 14 days to object to abandonment (P.R. LBR 6007-1(b);
// FRBP 6007(a)), the 28 days' service of a plan avoiding a lien and the 7
// days to object to confirmation (P.R. LBR 3015-3(c)(2), (d)(3); FRBP
// 2002(b), 3015(f)), the 180-day governmental bar date (P.R. LBR 3003-1; 11
// U.S.C. § 502(b)(9)) and the first chapter 13 plan payment within 30 days
// (P.R. LBR 2016-1(f); 11 U.S.C. § 1326(a)(1)).
//
// Layers, in date order: the Local Bankruptcy Rules' "complete list" (file
// PRLBRs-2013_Complete_2, undated; it already carries the 2018 text of
// P.R. LBR 3015-3 and 9013-1) is CURRENCY UNCONFIRMED (sources/bankr-pr/
// PROVENANCE.md): General Order 19-01 (June 28, 2019) is listed by the
// court but its link is dead and it is not vendored. So every period bound
// only to that file is declared with a hole cite naming its pinpoint, the
// value the vendored text's, unverified. General Order 17-08 (December 1,
// 2017) adopted P.R. LBR 3015-2 and Local Form G; General Orders 18-01 and
// 18-02, each "effective immediately" on June 19, 2018, adopted P.R. LBR
// 3015-3 (superseding 3015-2) and amended P.R. LBR 9013-1, and their
// periods bind to the orders' own text; the package runs from that date.
// General Order 26-01, "effective immediately" on August 5, 2026, adopted
// P.R. LBR 9019-1 and 9019-2, whose periods run from then.
//
// Stated in the rules but not declared: the monthly operating report due
// the 21st day of the next month and the quarterly post-confirmation
// reports (P.R. LBR 2015-2), calendar dates rather than periods; the
// mediator's status report every 30 days (P.R. LBR 9019-1(d)); the
// certificate of service on a stay motion "within seven (7) days", whose
// trigger the text does not name (P.R. LBR 4001-5(c)); the court's own
// acts (dismissal 30 days after an inactivity order, P.R. LBR 7055-2(b); a
// stay hearing within 30 days of the petition, P.R. LBR 4001-5(d); the 21
// days the court keeps jurisdiction after a dismissal becomes final, P.R.
// LBR 2016-1(f)); and the next-business-day certificates of service (P.R.
// LBR 3015-3(c)(3), (d)(2)(B), (i)(2)). A paper
// served by mail gets 3 more days under FRBP 9006(f), as the notice
// language says.
/// An order granting ex parte relief is served (P.R. LBR 9013-1(b)).
event ExParteOrderServed()
/// A motion requiring response-time language is served (P.R. LBR
/// 9013-1(c)(1)).
event MotionServed()
/// A motion to compromise is served (P.R. LBR 9013-1(c)(2)(A)).
event CompromiseMotionServed()
/// A motion or notice of intended sale is served (P.R. LBR
/// 9013-1(c)(2)(B)).
event SaleNoticeServed()
/// A motion to modify a plan after confirmation is served (P.R. LBR
/// 9013-1(c)(2)(C)).
event PlanModificationMotionServed()
/// A motion to dismiss a chapter 7, 12 or 13 case is served (P.R. LBR
/// 9013-1(c)(2)(D)).
event DismissalMotionServed()
/// The date set for the hearing on confirmation of a chapter 13 plan (P.R.
/// LBR 3015-3(d)).
event ConfirmationHearingScheduled()
/// The court denies confirmation of a chapter 13 plan (P.R. LBR 3015-3(g)).
event ConfirmationDenied()
/// The order confirming a chapter 13 plan is entered on the docket (P.R.
/// LBR 3015-3(h)).
event ConfirmationOrderEntered()
/// The court issues notice of intent to close a chapter 13 case without a
/// discharge for unverified domestic support obligations (P.R. LBR
/// 3015-3(k)).
event CloseWithoutDischargeNoticeIssued()
/// A court-ordered mediation concludes (P.R. LBR 9019-1(c)).
event MediationConcluded()
/// A non-judicial mediator is appointed by the order to mediate (P.R. LBR
/// 9019-1(f)).
event MediatorAppointed()
/// The date of the § 341 meeting of creditors (P.R. LBR 1007-1(e)).
event MeetingOfCreditorsScheduled()
/// The § 341 meeting of creditors is held (P.R. LBR 2003-1(a)).
event MeetingOfCreditorsHeld()
/// The § 341 meeting of creditors in a chapter 7 case is concluded or
/// closed (P.R. LBR 2003-1(a)).
event MeetingOfCreditorsConcluded()
/// The schedules of liabilities are filed in a chapter 11 case (P.R. LBR
/// 1007-1(f)).
event Chapter11SchedulesFiled()
/// A creditor scheduled as disputed, contingent or unliquidated is added to
/// previously filed chapter 11 schedules (P.R. LBR 1007-1(f)).
event DisputedCreditorAdded()
/// The debtor serves Local Form A on the disputed, contingent or
/// unliquidated creditors (P.R. LBR 1007-1(f)).
event DisputedCreditorNoticeServed()
/// The debtor serves a creditor added by amendment with the required notice
/// (P.R. LBR 1009-1).
event AddedCreditorNoticeServed()
/// An order granting substantive consolidation is entered (P.R. LBR
/// 1015-1(c)).
event ConsolidationGranted()
/// The court's notice of intent to dismiss for want of prosecution is
/// served (P.R. LBR 1017-2(a)).
event DismissalNoticeServed()
/// The date of a proposed Rule 2004 examination (P.R. LBR 2004-1(d)).
event ExaminationScheduled()
/// A motion for a Rule 2004 examination is served (P.R. LBR 2004-1(d)).
event ExaminationMotionServed()
/// The later of the commencement of the case and the date a professional
/// first rendered services (P.R. LBR 2014-1(e)).
event ProfessionalEngagementBegan()
/// A chapter 13 fee application of $500 or less lacking the debtor's and
/// trustee's approval is noticed (P.R. LBR 2016-1(f)).
event FeeApplicationNoticed()
/// An order dismissing a chapter 13 case with no plan confirmed becomes
/// final (P.R. LBR 2016-1(f)).
event UnconfirmedDismissalFinal()
/// An objection to a claim is served (P.R. LBR 3007-1(c)).
event ClaimObjectionServed()
/// A chapter 11 trustee is appointed (P.R. LBR 3016-1).
event TrusteeAppointed()
/// The date set for the hearing on confirmation of a chapter 11 plan (P.R.
/// LBR 3018-2).
event Chapter11ConfirmationHearingScheduled()
/// The order confirming a chapter 11 plan becomes final (P.R. LBR
/// 3022-1(b)).
event ConfirmationOrderFinal()
/// An application for a chapter 11 final decree is filed (P.R. LBR
/// 3022-1(d)).
event FinalDecreeApplicationFiled()
/// The notice of hearing on a motion for relief from stay is issued (P.R.
/// LBR 4001-1(c)).
event StayReliefNoticeIssued()
/// The movant serves the motion for relief from stay and the notice (P.R.
/// LBR 4001-1(c), (e)).
event StayReliefNoticeServed()
/// The date set in the notice for the hearing on a motion for relief from
/// stay (P.R. LBR 4001-1(g)).
event StayReliefHearingScheduled()
/// A motion to continue or impose the automatic stay under 11 U.S.C. §
/// 362(c)(3)(B) or (c)(4)(B) is filed (P.R. LBR 4001-5(c)).
event StayMotionFiled()
/// A motion to continue or impose the automatic stay is served (P.R. LBR
/// 4001-5(c)).
event StayMotionServed()
/// A motion to avoid a lien under 11 U.S.C. § 522(f) is served (P.R. LBR
/// 4003-2(c)).
event LienAvoidanceMotionServed()
/// A filing user receives the Notice of Electronic Filing (P.R. LBR
/// 5005-4(h)).
event ElectronicFilingNoticeReceived()
/// A motion to reopen a case is served (P.R. LBR 5010-1).
event ReopenMotionServed()
/// The date set for a hearing or trial (P.R. LBR 5071-1(a), 9074-1(a)).
event HearingScheduled()
/// The date set for a proposed use, sale or lease outside the ordinary
/// course of business (P.R. LBR 6004-1(c)).
event ProposedSaleDate()
/// A sale of estate property outside the ordinary course of business takes
/// place (P.R. LBR 6004-1(d)).
event SaleClosed()
/// A date set in an adversary scheduling order (P.R. LBR 7016-1(b)).
event ScheduledDate()
/// The date of the final pretrial conference in an adversary proceeding
/// (P.R. LBR 7016-1(c)).
event FinalPretrialConferenceScheduled()
/// The plaintiff or movant serves its portion of the Joint Pretrial Report
/// (P.R. LBR 7016-1(c)(1)).
event PretrialReportDraftServed()
/// The date an evidentiary hearing commences (P.R. LBR 7016-1(d)).
event EvidentiaryHearingScheduled()
/// An adversary matter is dismissed for the plaintiff's default on the FRCP
/// 26(f) requirements (P.R. LBR 7026-1).
event DismissedForNoncompliance()
/// An order giving notice that an inactive adversary proceeding will be
/// dismissed is entered (P.R. LBR 7055-2(a)).
event InactivityOrderEntered()
/// The date set for the hearing of a matter that is or becomes contested in
/// which an attorney appears pro hac vice without local counsel (P.R. LBR
/// 9010-1(b)).
event ContestedHearingScheduled()
/// The date the last responsive pleading is required to be filed in an
/// adversary proceeding (P.R. LBR 9015-1(a)).
event LastResponsivePleadingDue()
/// A notice of removal is filed under FRBP 9027 (P.R. LBR 9027-1(a)).
event RemovalNoticeFiled()
/// An electronic transcript is filed (P.R. LBR 9037-1(c)).
event TranscriptFiled()
/// The time for a notice of appeal from the court's decision elapses with
/// no appeal, or an appeal is finally determined (P.R. LBR 9070-1(d)).
event AppealPeriodEnded()

/// P.R. LBR 9013-1(b) (General Order 18-02): an affected party may request
/// a hearing on ex parte relief by a motion for review filed within 14 days
/// of service of the order.
deadline ex-parte-review-period: 14.days after ExParteOrderServed() counted_by frbp9006-puerto-rico cite "P.R. LBR (GO 18-02) 9013-1(b)"
/// P.R. LBR 9013-1(c)(1) (General Order 18-02): an objection or response to
/// a motion is served and filed within 14 days after service, plus 3 days
/// under FRBP 9006(f) if served by mail; otherwise the paper is deemed
/// unopposed.
deadline response-period: 14.days after MotionServed() counted_by frbp9006-puerto-rico cite "P.R. LBR (GO 18-02) 9013-1(c)"
/// P.R. LBR 9013-1(c)(2)(A) (General Order 18-02): the response time on a
/// motion to compromise is 21 days.
deadline compromise-response-period: 21.days after CompromiseMotionServed() counted_by frbp9006-puerto-rico cite "P.R. LBR (GO 18-02) 9013-1(c)"
/// P.R. LBR 9013-1(c)(2)(B) (General Order 18-02): the response time on a
/// motion or notice of intended sale is 21 days.
deadline sale-response-period: 21.days after SaleNoticeServed() counted_by frbp9006-puerto-rico cite "P.R. LBR (GO 18-02) 9013-1(c)"
/// P.R. LBR 9013-1(c)(2)(C) (General Order 18-02): the response time on a
/// motion to modify a plan after confirmation is 21 days.
deadline plan-modification-response-period: 21.days after PlanModificationMotionServed() counted_by frbp9006-puerto-rico cite "P.R. LBR (GO 18-02) 9013-1(c)"
/// P.R. LBR 9013-1(c)(2)(D) (General Order 18-02): the response time on a
/// motion to dismiss a chapter 7, 12 or 13 case is 30 days.
deadline dismissal-response-period: 30.days after DismissalMotionServed() counted_by frbp9006-puerto-rico cite "P.R. LBR (GO 18-02) 9013-1(c)"
/// P.R. LBR 3015-3(d)(4)(B) (General Order 18-01): if the § 341 meeting is
/// held within 7 days of the confirmation hearing, the trustee may file the
/// minutes with an objection not later than one day before the confirmation
/// hearing.
deadline trustee-minutes-period: 1.days before ConfirmationHearingScheduled() counted_by frbp9006-puerto-rico cite "P.R. LBR (GO 18-01) 3015-3(d)"
/// P.R. LBR 3015-3(d)(5) (General Order 18-01): if an objection to a
/// chapter 13 plan is filed 7 days before the confirmation hearing, the
/// debtor files a response, amending the plan or replying, not later than
/// one day before the hearing.
deadline objection-response-period: 1.days before ConfirmationHearingScheduled() counted_by frbp9006-puerto-rico cite "P.R. LBR (GO 18-01) 3015-3(d)"
/// P.R. LBR 3015-3(g)(1) (General Order 18-01): if confirmation is denied,
/// the court may dismiss the case unless within 14 days the debtor files an
/// amended plan, moves to convert, seeks to alter or amend the order under
/// FRBP 9023, or the court orders otherwise.
deadline confirmation-denial-cure-period: 14.days after ConfirmationDenied() counted_by frbp9006-puerto-rico cite "P.R. LBR (GO 18-01) 3015-3(g)"
/// P.R. LBR 3015-3(h)(2)(A) (General Order 18-01): where the plan provides
/// for compensation on an application, the debtor's attorney files it no
/// later than 14 days from the docket entry of the confirmation order.
deadline confirmation-fee-application-period: 14.days after ConfirmationOrderEntered() counted_by frbp9006-puerto-rico cite "P.R. LBR (GO 18-01) 3015-3(h)"
/// P.R. LBR 3015-3(k)(2) (General Order 18-01): the case closes without a
/// discharge unless within 14 days the debtor certifies under penalty of
/// perjury that all post-petition domestic support obligations are current.
deadline support-obligation-certification-period: 14.days after CloseWithoutDischargeNoticeIssued() counted_by frbp9006-puerto-rico cite "P.R. LBR (GO 18-01) 3015-3(k)"
/// P.R. LBR 9019-1(c)(1)(D) (General Order 26-01): the parties or the
/// mediator report the results of the mediation immediately on its
/// conclusion and not later than 14 days thereafter.
deadline mediation-report-period: 14.days after MediationConcluded() counted_by frbp9006-puerto-rico effective [2026-08-05, ..) cite "P.R. LBR (GO 26-01) 9019-1(c)"
/// P.R. LBR 9019-1(f)(3) (General Order 26-01): within 14 days of
/// appointment, a non-judicial mediator files a disclosure of conflicts and
/// prior service.
deadline mediator-disclosure-period: 14.days after MediatorAppointed() counted_by frbp9006-puerto-rico effective [2026-08-05, ..) cite "P.R. LBR (GO 26-01) 9019-1(f)"
/// P.R. LBR 1006-1(a): after $50.00 at filing, the balance of an
/// installment fee is paid in no more than 3 equal installments every 30
/// days thereafter.
deadline installment-period: 30.days after PetitionFiled() counted_by frbp9006-puerto-rico cite ?("P.R. LBR 1006-1(a), 2013 complete list: CURRENCY UNCONFIRMED against later general orders (GO 19-01 not vendored); the value is the vendored text, unverified") {}
/// P.R. LBR 1007-1(c)-(d): the statement of social security number,
/// corporate resolution, fee payment or application, creditor matrix,
/// 20-largest list and § 342(b) notice are filed within 2 days of the
